  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 26,
    "summary": "Honor is not fitting for a fool—Answer not a fool according to his folly—Where there is no talebearer, the strife ceases.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "As snow in summer, and as rain in harvest, so honour is not seemly for a fool.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "Prov. 12:9; D&C 121:35."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As the bird by wandering, as the swallow by flying, so the curse causeless shall not come.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A whip for the horse, a bridle for the ass, and a rod for the fool’s back.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Answer not a fool according to his folly, lest thou also be like unto him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he be wise in his own conceit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "Matt. 16:2 (1–4)."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "OR own eyes (also vv. 12, 16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that sendeth a message by the hand of a fool cutteth off the feet, and drinketh damage.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "OR violence, injury."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The legs of the lame are not equal: so is a parable in the mouth of fools.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As he that bindeth a stone in a sling, so is he that giveth honour to a fool.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As a thorn goeth up into the hand of a drunkard, so is a parable in the mouth of fools.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The great God that formed all things both rewardeth the fool, and rewardeth transgressors.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Reward."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As a dog returneth to his vomit, so a fool returneth to his folly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "2 Pet. 2:22; 3 Ne. 7:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Seest thou a man wise in his own conceit? there is more hope of a fool than of him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Rom. 11:25; 12:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "Prov. 29:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The slothful man saith, There is a lion in the way; a lion is in the streets.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As the door turneth upon his hinges, so doth the slothful upon his bed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The slothful hideth his hand in his bosom; it grieveth him to bring it again to his mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The sluggard is wiser in his own conceit than seven men that can render a reason.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 15
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that passeth by, and meddleth with strife belonging not to him, is like one that taketh a dog by the ears.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "Dogs were not pets in Israel, but typically ran wild; one seized by the ears would certainly bite its attacker."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 54
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As a mad man who casteth firebrands, arrows, and death,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So is the man that deceiveth his neighbour, and saith, Am not I in sport?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "D&C 10:25 (25–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Where no wood is, there the fire goeth out: so where there is no talebearer, the strife ceaseth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Gossip."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "Alma 4:9 (8–9); 16:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As coals are to burning coals, and wood to fire; so is a contentious man to kindle strife.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "TG Contention."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The words of a talebearer are as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Burning lips and a wicked heart are like a potsherd covered with silver dross.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "IE a broken piece of an earthen vessel."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that hateth dissembleth with his lips, and layeth up deceit within him;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Hate."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Deceit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When he speaketh fair, believe him not: for there are seven abominations in his heart.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Ps. 28:3; Isa. 9:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whose hatred is covered by deceit, his wickedness shall be shewed before the whole congregation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Alma 14:3 (2–3); 37:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso diggeth a pit shall fall therein: and he that rolleth a stone, it will return upon him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Prov. 28:10; 1 Ne. 14:3; 22:14; 2 Ne. 28:8; D&C 109:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A lying tongue hateth those that are afflicted by it; and a flattering mouth worketh ruin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Gossip."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Flatter."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
